# SAEA-E-004F — A-1a boundary-policy contrast on the FAST split (owner
# sampling-ratio authorization 2026-08-11; ≤30-min-per-task phase rule).
#
# The E-004 design (wave1-e21-sub5, one shared control, three contrasts)
# stands for the full pass; this fast pair is DIRECTIONAL — and it carries
# two engineering stakes beyond the WER question: fixed windows make slice
# audio RUN-INVARIANT, which (a) removes the model-boundary cascade that
# drives the measured run-to-run noise, and (b) is the enabler for the
# owner's audio-feature-cache design (encode once per slice, reuse across
# arms/runs — impossible while boundaries drift).
#
# Both arms under locked A-prime. The control doubles as the A-prime-era
# bare-core floor on this split (all prior bare-core fast runs were A-era).
# Read: WER delta (vs the noise band; the a1a hypothesis is model-boundary
# >= 1 pp better), boundary-tier histogram, slice-count/audio-total delta
# (fixed windows have NO overlap: ~17% less audio per pass).
#
# run_id:baseline_fragment
SAEA-E-004F-a1a-control:bare-core-ojw
SAEA-E-004F-a1a-fixedwindow:a1a-fixed-window-ojw
